      "writtenOn": "2023-03-15T18:15:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That\u0027s a good question. glslang still supports the old format when the version is set to Vulkan 1.0 and Tint handles both old and 1.3 formats (I remember when I ran into this during the exploration sprint I was referred to this bug that suggests both formats are valid: https://bugs.chromium.org/p/tint/issues/detail?id\u003d1648#c1). \n\nI\u0027m not aware of a particular disadvantage or benefit to using one or the other. I imagine SPV_KHR_variable_pointers is the main use case (https://htmlpreview.github.io/?https://github.com/KhronosGroup/SPIRV-Registry/blob/master/extensions/KHR/SPV_KHR_variable_pointers.html) for Vulkan. The newer version requires SPIR-V 1.3, SPV_KHR_storage_buffer_storage_class, or SPV_KHR_variable_pointers.\n\nI updated the `StorageBuffer.sksl` test to both read and write to a storage buffer and passes validation just using `Uniform + BufferBlock` (whereas it wouldn\u0027t with `Uniform + Block`). Both the SPIR-V and the HLSL seem to do the right thing.\n\nFor our purposes, since we validate SPIR-V Vulkan 1.0 target-env version we currently have to use the old format.",
      "parentUuid": "b451c6f6_4e530d7e",
